    gas_offer_margin_anchor_vintage: { cell: "R", ev: "pjm-169 (2026-09-07) — BUILT, SCREENED, and REJECTED by its own pre-registered STOP gate S4. One-year screen (2022, chosen on FOOTPRINT before any solve) on the F2-armed keeper recipe, single declared delta, control = this session's own F2-armed 2022 touchpoint at the SAME HEAD (G-CTRL form 4; G-DRIFT discharged by construction, zero control LP spent). S1 identity PASS (resolved anchor 7.1208 vs the census's 2022 _gas_series mean 7.120797). S2 PASS (mc delta = 0 exactly at fuel == anchor; 8 unit tests). S3 PASS: +$10.57/MWh median gas-tranche shift against a +$10.58 prediction FIXED IN THE PRECOMMIT BEFORE THE SOLVE — ratio 0.999, 981 tranches both sides, P1 objective 19.433e9 -> 20.137e9. S4 FAIL: COAL_BIT +3.28% (+4.55 TWh), COAL_PRB +7.09%, COAL_WC +3.31% against a 1.0% bar. S5 PASS (C1 FAIL->FAIL, C2/C4 PASS->PASS). KILL RULE APPLIED: the remaining years were NEVER spent and nothing is promoted. REPORTED, NOT GATED, AND NOT A RESCUE (rule 1 [R-STRUCT]): C1 2022 CC_REGULAR improves +22.02 -> +10.77 TWh and C3b 0.257 -> 0.243 — an arm killed on structure is not revived by a target improving. HONEST CAVEAT ON THE GATE ITSELF: S4 probably cannot separate the coal-sigmoid confound it was written for from ordinary merit-order displacement (raising every gas offer $10.57/MWh MUST push dispatch to the next unit up, which in PJM is coal). The verdict STANDS regardless — rule 29(c) fixes gates before the solve precisely so they cannot be re-read once a number is on the table. A future charter may re-specify a displacement-aware footprint gate, but only in its OWN precommit, before its OWN solve, re-running the screen from scratch. THE STRONGER LEAD IS ELSEWHERE and is untouched by this rejection: PJM bituminous sits on its COAL_SIGMOID_DEFAULTS ceil asymptote in 91.5% of 2022 hours against 0.0% in 2023 AND 2024 — a larger, better-evidenced window extrapolation pointing the OPPOSITE way, and its own card under rule 19. Screen bundles deleted before merge (rule 29c). Evidence: docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-pjm169-f4-anchor-vintage-2026-09-06.md §7 (census) and §9 (gate table)." },
    gas_offer_margin_zonal_anchor_vintage: { cell: "U", ev: "row minted nyiso-230 (2026-09-12) with NYISO's measured defect; BUILT, default-off and byte-identical off. Whether this ISO can reach the gate at all depends on its zonal-basis applier: PJM / ERCOT / MISO re-centre on the GAS-CAPACITY-weighted fleet mean, so the resolver REFUSES them rather than mis-measure with a synthetic probe — reaching them is a build task (resolve against the year's real fleet), not an arming decision. CAISO carries an applier and no capacity weighting in the derive's own classification, so it is reachable once its lane wants it; NEISO and SPP carry no zonal applier, so the ISO-level gas_offer_margin_anchor_vintage is their flag instead. Every ISO carries the SAME construction in kind — a frozen 2023-2025 window mean applied to whatever year is solved — and it is each lane's to adjudicate on its own market's data (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]): no NYISO verdict fills this cell, and NYISO has minted none." },
