    diurnal_price_amplitude: { cell: "G", ev: "pjm-139/140/141 + matrix item 13; xiso-1 §2 reconciles pjm-141's 31/33/32 % to 31.6/36.5/34.2 %. pjm-163 promotion re-stamp (2026-08-16, rule 28 / finding §4): the DEBUG-B input-clock repair moves this family's evidence basis — 2023/24 fueltype series (solar/wind CF shapes, gas benchmark) shift +1h, so the cited amplitude magnitudes were measured at the PRE-repair inputs and stand as historical record under the pjm-152-era keeper; the G verdict (owner-closed frontier, no admissible in-model route) is NOT re-adjudicated and is input-clock-independent — the flat-stack representation boundary is unchanged by a 1h re-placement | pjm-171 (2026-09-07, ZERO LP) EXTENDS THE EVIDENCE, does NOT re-adjudicate: the G verdict stands and no lever is proposed. The flat-stack defect is now measured across the FULL 2021-2025 span (pjm-141 had 2023-2025) on the LOAD axis, and it is what PJM 2021 C3a +10.8% IS. Per-year C3a gap ($/MWh) split into a TROUGH leg (load deciles 1-8) and a PEAK leg (d9-10): 2021 +3.56/+0.57, 2022 +4.24/-11.87, 2023 +3.42/-1.72, 2024 +2.28/-2.73, 2025 +0.82/-4.54. The trough leg is POSITIVE IN ALL FIVE YEARS including the three tuned ones; the peak leg is the year-varying term and it sets C3a's SIGN. 2021 is the only year whose peak leg is ~0 (its decile-10 actual is $56.55 vs $172.00/2022, $48.28/2023, $62.10/2024, $92.67/2025), so the trough surplus stands alone and the defect reads at full magnitude. STRUCTURAL SIGNATURE, year-invariant: bottom-decile implied market heat rate (price / the model's OWN _gas_series) is 8.46/7.92/8.71/9.28/9.17 model vs 6.55/5.87/6.02/6.35/7.01 actual (2021-2025) — the model's overnight margin is a CC at rated heat rate in every year, PJM's clears BELOW any CC's full-load heat rate. NO SINGLE-ENDED REPAIR SURVIVES (the new decision-grade result): closing the trough alone sends 2022 to -16.0%, closing the peak alone sends TRAINING YEAR 2023 to +11.5% — both outside the +/-10% commercial band, and robust at split deciles 7/8/9. So the cancellation pjm-141 named is LOAD-BEARING IN THE TUNED WINDOW, not only in the held-out years, and any admissible repair must move BOTH ends. DO-NOT-REDO REAFFIRMED: do not open a card to close 2021 on a level lever — rule 30(c) holds PJM CALIBRATED, rule 22 forbids quoting 2021 as skill, and every single-ended lever regresses a passing year. Evidence: results/calibration/FINDING-pjm171-2021-c3a-is-the-flat-stack-without-its-offset-2026-09-07.md" },
