    benchmark_membership_vintage_union: { cell: "O", ev: "SPP-49 (2026-09-19) cross-ISO census \u2014 O: OPEN, and PJM is BY FAR THE LARGEST EXPOSURE IN THE PROGRAM, for a SEPARATE reason that deserves its own charter rather than this flag's. PJM is NOT a member of zone_assignment._EIA860_SUPPLEMENT_ISOS at all, so its benchmark membership is eGRID-2023-ONLY with no EIA-860 supplement of any kind: 1,727 plants in the lookup against 2,584 in the EIA-860 PJM-BA union \u2014 857 missing. Measured at ROW grain, the union would add EIA-923 generation in EVERY year including live keeper years: 2020 +10,045,593 MWh (113 rows), 2021 +8,999,931 (82), 2022 +4,933,185 (54), 2023 +97 (8), 2024 +2,452,964 (138), 2025 +8,804,034 (47). 8.8 TWh absent from the 2025 ACTUAL is on 2026-09-11-pjm-d4-4-gasoutage's own scored span. NOTHING IS ARMED and no verdict is transferred (rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d)): SPP's measurement fills no cell here, and PJM's own lane must decide whether the right repair is this union or simply adding PJM to the supplement set \u2014 they are different objects with different blast radii, and the 2024/2025 half is post-eGRID new build rather than mid-window retirees. Recorded now so it is not rediscovered." },
