    coal_offer_net_revenue_margin: { cell: "U", ev: "pjm-146 (2026-08-02, no solve) — cell stays U, INSTRUMENT-BLOCKED for the ERCOT form: the identification reads the 60-Day SCED Submitted TPO disclosure (per-unit, identity-resolved); PJM's DataMiner2 energy-offers corpus is unit-masked (PJM-NUC-1b: base64-opaque unit_code; pjm-128: no public unit-level DA award feed). A PJM-instrument CLASS-level variant is not barred by the measured_offer_surface R (that adjudicated the SURFACE use) but needs masked-identity capacity-weighting, the pjm-126/127 conditioning lesson, and a rule-19 replacement design vs the armed owners — a chartered DOF-retirement lane, not a single lever (docs/handoffs/pjm-matrix-column-triage-2026-08.md §2.4) --- RE-MEASURED 2026-09-12 by pjm-h2 (docs/FINDING-pjm-h2b-coal-cc-object-2026-09-12.md; ZERO LP, nothing armed, no solve). CELL STAYS U AND THE INSTRUMENT BLOCK IS CONFIRMED CORRECT FOR THE FIELD AS IMPLEMENTED: it is scoped to the CAMPD coal _mustrun (min-load) tranche only and requires coal_offer_margin_level, the 60-Day SCED Submitted TPO-Price1 cap-wtd p50 -- an ERCOT disclosure PJM's unit-masked DataMiner2 corpus cannot serve. WHAT IS NEW: a DIFFERENT construction on the SAME seam is not instrument-blocked, and PJM already uses its instrument. PJM's registered offer_curve_by_group carries measured phys_* keys for its GAS bands that reproduce data/raw/reference/pjm_campd_marginal_hr_summary.csv BYTE FOR BYTE (CC_REGULAR phys_committed 1.015 = avg_committed_p50, phys_econ_low 0.87 = marg_econ_low_p50, phys_econ_high 1.052 = marg_econ_high_p50), while COAL_BIT carries NO phys_* key at all -- so under scenarios.py's own rule (a band without its phys_* key is neutral) PJM coal keeps the FULLY FUEL-SCALED multiplicative markup that gas_offer_net_revenue_margin (cell K, armed in the keeper at anchor 3.3483) exists to retire. The same artifact's COAL row is committed and unused: avg_committed_p50 0.916, marg_econ_low_p50 0.803, marg_econ_high_p50 0.809 against registered COAL_BIT multipliers 0.548/0.6556/1.2664. Because PJM coal's offer is keyed to GAS through the passthrough sigmoid, its above-physical markup swings x0.674 (2020) to x1.315 (2022) where a real plant's start/no-load hurdle is a $/MWh quantity. THIS IS A BUILD, NOT AN ARM (rule 28(c): new gate + matrix row in the same PR), and it does NOT reach a solve until the pre-solve offer-array delta is computed and fixed in a PRECOMMIT (rule 29 clause 0). ALSO KILLED AT ZERO LP BY THE SAME SESSION, so no successor spends an LP on them: the coal sigmoid FULL RE-DERIVATION (the committed derived row {floor 0.50, ceil 1.00, gas_mid 7.08, slope 1.0} moves coal CHEAPER in all six years -- 0.649/0.725/0.951/0.665/0.663/0.738 -- so it moves 2020 the WRONG WAY and risks the 8/8 keeper's 2023/2024 coal); the coal sigmoid CEILING (2022 already sits at x1.315 with 74.8% of hours on the ceiling asymptote and coal is STILL +8.0 TWh over on the 923 basis, so lowering it makes the miss worse, reproducing pjm-170); retiree_vintage_status_scope (drops 7.5 MW of PJM coal in EVERY year); PARTIAL DERATES / capability loss for COAL (per-plant CEMS p99.5 capability is FLAT across all six years on every unit, e.g. plant 3944 1937/1940/1934/1946/1941/1940 MW -- the same verdict pjm-h1 reached for CC, now extended to coal); FORCING (D-2 coal forced share 0.6-1.4% in 2020-2022 vs 4.0-4.1% in 2023-2024, LEAST where the surplus is largest); and OUTAGE-EXTRACT COVERAGE (PJM coal outage MW-days flat at 20.4/18.4/18.5 GW-equiv in 2020-2022 vs 20.9/16.8/15.5 in 2023-2025 -- the bad years carry MORE detected outage). THE SURVIVING EXPLANATION IS ROUTED, NOT OPENED: price-distribution compression (D-A amplitude 29.9-32.9% of measured in every year) inside the owner-declared-closed pjm-142 frontier, corroborating pjm-h1 and extending it from CC_REGULAR to coal." },
