    gas_electric_power_monthly_level: { cell: "K", ev: "KEEPER-CANDIDATE, SOLVED AND REGISTERED (pjm-fuelvintage-1, 2026-09-09; run 2026-09-09-pjm-fuelvintage-ep-level, bundle results/calibration/pjm_fuelvintage_A; docs/PRECOMMIT-pjm-fuelvintage-2026-09-09.md + docs/RESULT-pjm-fuelvintage-2026-09-09.md). PROMOTED UNDER THE OWNER RULING 2026-09-09 (verbatim: 'these should be promoted as keepers on both 860 and gas shape counts regardless of inertness'), and it is NOT inert in PJM. PHASE-0 CENSUS, the number the whole arm turned on: the keeper's F923 per-plant print path (gas_plant_monthly_fuel_pricing=True, nearby_fuel_price_fallback=True) owns only 51.794% of PJM gas capacity-hours in 2023 (1,744 gas rows / 100,451.1 MW; 780 rows / 47,285.5 MW owned in all 8,760 h; 844 rows / 46,825.4 MW - 46.6% of gas capacity - NEVER touched). The A2 prediction that the print path would render this arm inert (MISO's cell records 100% print ownership) is FALSE for PJM: ~48% of the gas fleet prices off the seam directly. ZERO-LP GATES, all three PASS before any solve: G-1 capacity-weighted gas array 3.0827 -> 2.7105 $/MMBtu (-0.3721), DOWN in 12/12 months, 964/1,744 rows and 53,165.6 MW moving; G-2 non-gas fuel prices move EXACTLY 0.0 (2,045 rows) and non-coal-non-gas OFFERS move exactly 0.0 (1,492 rows / 81,420 MW); G-3 the armed ISO _gas_series monthly means equal iso_electric_power_monthly_level('PJM',2023) to 0.0000000000 in 12/12 months - REPLACED, never blended (rule 19). A no-free-parameter identity confirms census and seam together: ISO-series delta -0.7746 x (1 - 0.51794) = -0.3734 predicted vs -0.3721 measured, 0.3% agreement. THE COAL DIRECTION WAS PRE-REGISTERED FROM THE OFFER ARRAYS AND THE HANDOFF'S PREDICTION WAS WRONG: two channels push opposite ways - direct (cheaper gas displaces coal, coal DOWN) vs indirect (the ISO _gas_series keys the coal PRB passthrough sigmoid, coal UP). Measured at zero LP: the coal offer falls -3.057 $/MWh (23.782 -> 20.725, -12.85%, 393/553 rows, 33,156.4 MW) while gas falls -3.259, so the coal-minus-gas gap moves +0.202 AGAINST coal. Predicted coal ~ flat with a slight DOWNWARD bias, against the handoff/FINDING §5b 'coal UP'. CONFIRMED BY THE SOLVE: coal -0.57% / -2.03% / +1.42% across 2023/2024/2025. SCREEN (2023, named ex ante on the largest measured footprint, mae 0.775 $/MMBtu): ALL FIVE STOP GATES PASS, G-5 slack and dump exactly 0.0. FULL SPAN 2023-2025, ONE invocation, ONE bundle (rule 16): EVERY scored criterion PASSES - C1 (D-10 free-class 16/16 all, 12/12 free), C2, C3a, C3b, C3c, C4, C6 - with zero caveats. C3b, the pre-registered highest-risk criterion in the program and the one that killed ercot-254, PASSES in all three years (PJM is the only in-scope ISO with no hub overlay, so the full move lands, and the move is 4.6x non-uniform across months; the protections that held are the 1.42 $/MMBtu max monthly gap vs ERCOT's 49.53, and gas_daily_shape already armed). C3a REPORTED AT FULL MAGNITUDE INCLUDING ITS COSTS: load-weighted model vs bench RT actual, 2023 31.4124 (+10.45%) -> 29.0536 (+2.16%); 2024 31.1074 (+5.34%) -> 29.6929 (+0.55%); 2025 42.3790 (-1.19%) -> 41.6390 (-2.92%) - two years markedly better, 2025 WORSE because the keeper was already under actual there. The 2023 move also OVERSHOT this session's own pre-registered -0.5 to -2.0 $/MWh band at -2.3587. Per rule 1 [R-STRUCT] none of this is why the cell is K: it lands on rule 14 [R-ACCURATE] as the measured delivered gas price, and it would land if C3a had worsened. ZERO free parameters (rule 21): DOF ledger carried VERBATIM at n_entries 19 / n_residual 6; weights are a rule-23 frozen EIA-860 derive, the conversion is EIA's published 1.036 MMBtu/Mcf, and the two admission conditions were declared ex ante and NEVER swept. No authorized_price_tuning block - this is not an offer-curve band multiplier. CONTROL POSTURE, a NEGATIVE result stated not papered over: G-DRIFT (rule 29(b)) is NOT RUNNABLE for PJM - the keeper git_sha 457ae04 is dead (pre-2026-08-16 rewrite, no citation-commit-map entry; pjm-177 concluded identically the same day) and the nearest surrogate base acf784ec is 221 files / 187,385 insertions from HEAD. pjm-177 MEASURED live drift (CT_PEAKER -2.34%, all else <=0.25%), so form 4 was used but DECLARED IMPAIRED with drift bands +/-0.25% (+/-2.4% CT_PEAKER) pre-registered before solving; COAL_BIT +0.10% and CT_PEAKER +0.07% fall inside them and are reported as NOT SEPARABLE. NO CONTROL SOLVE WAS SPENT. ESCALATED, NOT ABSORBED - C8 FAILS on 2025 ST_GAS (41.3% forced, D-4 provenance fail on st_netload_drag, a mechanism this seam never touches) AND IT IS NOT THIS ARM'S: the keeper's committed diagnostics carry 12 D-4 rows while HEAD's generator produces ~210, and the INCUMBENT KEEPER REGENERATED AT HEAD fails D-4 MORE than the arm (38 vs 35 failures) and re-scores CALIBRATED -> NOT-YET / C8 FAIL. PJM's designated keeper does not survive its own C8 gate under the diagnostics generator now on main - a pre-existing latent condition on main, surfaced here, routed to PJM's own lane as its own charter. The 2019-2022 EIA-860 retiree window (commit 7934e92c) is carried and is PROVEN INERT across this span: all 205 PJM rows it adds carry planned_retirement_year <= 2022, so 0 rows / 0.0 MW reach 2023/2024/2025 (per-year additions 13,294.9 / 8,094.5 / 5,687.1 / 4,535.9 MW for 2019-2022, 80.1% Conventional Steam Coal). The A5-item-2 partial-plant double-count cannot occur: partial_plant_exit_carry is absent from the keeper recipe (False)." },
