    seam_neighbour_anchored_ladder: { cell: "U", ev: "Untested for PJM (rule 25). PJM_SEAM_LADDER_BY_YEAR carries the same own-hub anchoring the miso-225 row names as the defect, so the cell is genuinely open -- but the verdict must be derived from PJM's own market data, never transferred." },
    seam_neighbour_hourly_ladder: { cell: "O", ev: "pjm-174 (2026-09-08) — cell U -> O. The PJM field pjm_seam_neighbour_hourly_ladder is BUILT (default off, byte-identical off, zero fitted parameters, table pinned to its derive by test) and SCREENED on 2025; it CLEARS ALL FIVE pre-registered gates and is therefore NOT KILLED — which under rule 29 [R-SCREEN] is exactly and only that: a screen may kill an arm, never promote one. NOT PROMOTED, NOT REGISTERED; keeper 2026-08-15-pjm-162-inputclock and PJM CALIBRATED untouched (rule 30(c)). THE CHARTERED HYPOTHESIS WAS REFUTED FIRST, ZERO-LP: PJM_SEAM_LADDER_BY_YEAR's band PRICES are right — the incumbent ladder reproduces its OWN basis (measured DA) to -0.046 TWh (2022) and -0.011 (2021) against total interchange misses of -10.127 / -14.382, at per-seam duration RMSE 42-274 MW inside the derivation's own claimed 40-280 MW band. THE DEFECT IS THE ANCHORING, as this row names it: a fixed annual price ladder on the ISO's OWN hub is a Q-Q coupling to the MEASURED price duration curve that the LP clears against the MODEL's, so fed the model's own price it loses -5.735 / -12.699 TWh of net export (57 % / 88 % of each year's miss), decomposing monotonically by measured-DA decile (d1 dPrice +11.98 -> dExport -3.308; d10 -48.48 -> +1.860). PROOF the band prices are not in it: quantile-mapping the model price onto the measured DA marginal distribution, hourly ranking untouched, and feeding the UNCHANGED ladder returns 31.732 / 37.805 TWh — the measured volume exactly. The per-border envelope is NOT the constraint (89.9 TWh of ceiling against 31.8 measured). GATES (all bars fixed in the PRECOMMIT before any solve): S1 identity max|mc-law| = 0 exactly on all 32 covered and all 48 uncovered rows; S2 byte-identical off; S3 footprint exactly 32 rows move, 0 non-seam, 0 of 48 SERC; S4 net export 23.270 -> 25.070, +1.800 TWh, inside the pre-registered [+1.0,+7.0] band; S5 zero collateral flips. A/B on the keeper's frozen recipe, BOTH LEGS AT HEAD 5e3b6c6a, one declared delta; P0 objective 10.948e9 -> 11.965e9 and P1 11.302e9 -> 12.330e9, so the mechanism is no no-op. REPORTED AT FULL MAGNITUDE AND AGAINST THE ARM (rules 1/29, gating nothing): the realised +1.800 TWh is HALF the pre-registered +3.591 band-clearing prediction (ratio 0.501), a larger over-statement than the ~20-25 % the phase-0 decomposition records; the aggregate interchange hourly r vs the tie-line meter gets WORSE, +0.587 -> +0.556, so readout A's per-seam shape repair did NOT survive aggregation into the LP net position and this card does not claim it did; and the extra export is bought with PEAKING GAS (CT_PEAKER +1.192 TWh, ST_GAS +0.251, CC_REGULAR -0.196). C3a moves TOWARD the band (-3.51 -> -2.89 where the control replay moves away to -3.54) and gates nothing. Zero-carbon classes move +0.000, as a seam-only mechanism must. The one non-load-bearing move (forced_share 2025 ST_GAS PASS -> FAIL) appears IDENTICALLY in the CONTROL's own gate run and is a replay artifact common to both legs — which is why the same-HEAD control was spent: G-DRIFT 22eda76a -> 5e3b6c6a found TWO LIVE hunks (f923_gas_price_plausibility_screen, default True and reachable on PJM's backcast gates; and EGRID_CT_HR_PHYSICAL_FLOOR, observed firing on ~20 PJM GT/IC plants in this session's own log), voiding G-CTRL form 4. NOT A KEEPER ON THIS EVIDENCE and structurally cannot be: a 2025-only screen bundle, and rule 16 [R-ALLYEARS] forbids a single-year keeper — promotion needs a full 2023-2025 span (~35-70 min LP), which is the open owner-facing question. The repair is PARTIAL: +1.800 TWh of a -9.655 TWh 2025 miss (~19 %), leaving the price-duration-curve error and the ~4 TWh application-geometry residual untouched. NOTE the miss is NOT a holdout artefact — the keeper's own 2025 TRAINING year is -9.692 TWh on the same signature. Anchors named on TOPOLOGY before deriving (rule 14); MISO system-hub sensitivity selects nothing; coverage is full-or-omit (MISO absent 2019/2021 and 2022 on ONE contiguous 525 h zonal-DA outage), every omission degrading to the incumbent, never to an unpriced seam (rule 19). NO VERDICT TRANSFERRED (rule 25): every parameter derived from PJM's own market data. Screen year 2025 fixed on MEASURED FOOTPRINT before any solve and it is a TRAINING year, so NO holdout authorization was spent and no out-of-training year was solved, scored or registered. Screen bundles gitignored, never registered (rule 29c), and NOT deleted (rule 31 [R-RETAIN]). Evidence: results/calibration/FINDING-pjm174-seam-ladder-anchoring-2026-09-08.md; card docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-pjm174-seam-neighbour-hourly-ladder-2026-09-08.md'  || FULL SPAN SOLVED AND NOT PROMOTED (2026-09-09, owner ruling). pjm175_span_arm, --year 2023 2024 2025, ONE bundle (rule 16), mechanism armed in all three years. EVERY load-bearing criterion PASSES (C1/C2/C3a/C3b) and so do C3c and C4; screen_collateral_gate vs the keeper reads 0 FLIPS across all three years with per-class moves predominantly TOWARD actuals. Net export improves in ALL THREE years (+1.430 / +0.789 / +1.837 TWh; span miss -34.574 -> -30.518). THE OWNER RULED IT NOT PROMOTABLE AND THE RULING IS CORRECT ON THE EVIDENCE: the mechanism's OWN central structural claim is contradicted by the solve. It is justified by the seam clearing on the SPREAD because the neighbour's supply cost is the real driver, so hourly response should improve; readout A predicted exactly that on the measured record (NYISO +0.235 -> +0.723) and the LP delivered the OPPOSITE in all three years (r 0.632->0.593, 0.626->0.510, 0.588->0.556). A volume improvement without its mechanism confirmed is not structurally more correct — it is a volume adjustment that happens to move the right way, which is exactly what rule 1 [R-STRUCT] exists to refuse. NOT THE REASON, recorded so it is not re-litigated: (a) the C8 forced_share FAIL (2025 ST_GAS 48.6 %, D-4 conduct FAIL on st_netload_drag plants 3131/3138/3148/3775/593) is NOT this mechanism's — the same-HEAD control with the mechanism OFF reads 50.6 % against the registered keeper's grounded 39.9 %, so both replays fail and the ARM IS MARGINALLY BETTER; it is a replay-path artifact. (b) C6 was UNATTESTED only because a replay bundle carries no attestation — procedural, not substantive. Per-border-link check reported INCONCLUSIVE by its own weakness: 4 of 5 external->border links improve (EMAAC +0.011, ATSI +0.069, AEP-Ohio +0.073, Dominion +0.020; ComEd -0.016) while the aggregate net position degrades -0.123, but every |r| < 0.26 and the zone->seam mapping is approximate. DISPOSITION: keeper 2026-08-15-pjm-162-inputclock and PJM CALIBRATED unchanged; run registered then pruned to keeper-only retention; bundles deleted under rule 31 [R-RETAIN] trigger (i), the owner having ruled FIRST. The field stays in main, DEFAULT OFF and byte-identical off, table + tests + derive pin intact — available to a successor that can demonstrate the hourly claim, costing nothing while unarmed." },
