    dam_availability_rebasis: { cell: "G", ev: "pjm-145 (refused ex ante, no solve; FINDING-pjm145-dam-availability-2026-08-02.md; PREREG-pjm145-dam-availability-2026-08-02.md; _pjm145_damavail_exante.json + _pjm145_damavail_decompose.json). STAYS G, and pjm-162 CLOSES its re-open condition (1) ex ante, no solve: the restore-ceiling form is ANTI-TARGETED — the water-fill's net direction is RESTORE on every year, both bases and every slice INCLUDING top-1% net-load days (+10.4/+12.4/+7.0 GW) and the named winter events (+7.6/+9.2/+2.2 GW), i.e. it gives capacity BACK exactly where pjm-161 measured the envelope is already too shallow. Cause is a CAPACITY-BASE gap the ercot137 ceiling cannot reach: 19.2-20.4% of model fossil nameplate sits at HARD ZERO every day (layup / retiree CEMS cap / COD mask / full windows), which PJM's published record does not carry as outage at all; the ceiling removes only ~60% of the restore lift (58.8/60.8/60.6% structural-zero) and 5.4-6.9 GW of live-unit restore survives it. FINDING-pjm162-outage-envelope-basis-closure-2026-08-15.md; _pjm162_route1_phase0.json" },
    pjm_measured_outage_event_cap: { cell: "R", ev: "pjm-161 pre-registered A/B, both arms registered (2026-08-14-pjm-161-control / -event-cap): P4 FAILED OUTRIGHT (C3c hours>$200 3/10/32 UNCHANGED, max price identical) and P6 top-1%-netload unavailable MW unchanged 23160->23160 / 25403->25403 / 24222->24249 — the cap adds ~zero outage in the hours it was built for. KEEPER ADJUDICATION against the owner standing standard (structural gain may carry a keeper even where gates regress): NOT A KEEPER, and the premise is what fails rather than the gates — NO gate regresses (both arms C1 16/16 free 12/12, all criteria PASS) and several class errors improve, but the model already asserts MORE fossil-thermal outage (41.7/43.2/41.2 GW annual mean) than PJM publishes for its ENTIRE fleet (33.3/33.0/35.9 GW), so a remove-only cap moves the LEVEL away from the operator record while moving the SHAPE toward it only in mid-load hours. The favourable residuals therefore come from an effect the justification does not cover (rule 1). Keeper stays 2026-08-04-pjm-152-collapse. FINDING §7.5. PREREG-pjm161-measured-outage-event-cap-2026-08-14.md; FINDING-pjm161-outage-inversion-and-da-virtual-energy-2026-08-14.md §7; results/calibration/_pjm161_ab.json" },
