    eia860_vintage_tracks_solve_year: { cell: "R", ev: "pjm-168 (2026-09-06): SCREENED and REJECTED. Arm-vs-control, same HEAD b5925d26, 2021 only, gates as fixed in PRECOMMIT-pjm167-fleet-vintage-screen-2026-09-06.md \u00a74. Six of seven gates PASS, G1 to the megawatt (arm COAL registry 48,708.3 / control 38,722.3 MW; the whole \u00a73.3 census reproduces inside the solve path, and the control loads 1,922 generators against the arm\u0027s 2,124). KILLED by G3: the +9,986 MW of restored nameplate produced NO headroom \u2014 the model spent it, +9,342 MW of peak coal dispatch (36,955 \u2192 46,297) and +29.18 TWh, staying pinned at 95.0 % of its own ceiling against 95.4 % before. PJM 2021 is NOT coal-capacity-bound: the model runs coal to whatever rail it is given, and with the correct registry it OVERSHOOTS the EIA-930 metered coal peak by +3,619 MW and overshoots two of the three coal bases on energy (+16.23 TWh classFull, +24.28 CEMS) while landing -2.10 on EIA-930. The fleet-vintage defect itself is real and unrefuted; what G3 refutes is that repairing it repairs the 2021 miss \u2014 the object is the coal-vs-gas offer ordering (F4). Step 2 (the 2023-2025 protective re-solve) was NEVER spent, per the kill rule. Nothing promoted; keeper unchanged. Evidence: results/calibration/FINDING-pjm168-f1-f2-screens-2026-09-06.md \u00a71. DO NOT REDO without new evidence." },
    pjm_interface_feed_admissibility_gate: { cell: "K", ev: "pjm-169 (2026-09-06/07) — **ARMED FOR PJM** by owner decision 2026-09-06 on the pjm-168 screen (which cleared 6/6). Cell moves O -> K: the mechanism is armed in the DESIGNATED KEEPER'S RECIPE (2026-08-15-pjm-162-inputclock). ARMED IN pipeline/backcast_config.py, NOT in iso_configs._pjm_config default_scenario_overrides as the handoff prescribed — that site is applied by runner.run_scenario_iso, the FORECAST front end, and the backcast lane reaches the LP through run_calibration.run_year + pipeline.solve and never calls apply_iso_scenario_defaults at all (runner.py:1261-64; no call site in run_calibration*.py). Arming there would have RECORDED the flag and changed nothing in the LP — the caiso-162 defect class. Both of the D57/D67/D75-R arming conditions hold and are MEASURED: PJM armed 20bc47b308268183, PJM --no-pjm-interface-feed-admissibility-gate 6595f6053397d5a0 = IDENTICAL to the pre-arm HEAD key, and ERCOT/CAISO/MISO/NYISO/NEISO byte-identical (rule 25). The --no- form is NEW: F2 shipped from pjm-167 with no CLI flag at all, so an armed run had no way back; threaded tri-state on the ct_netload_drag pattern, and because recorded_cfg starts from backcast_config, run_config.json reports the ARMED posture for an unset caller (rule 24). IN-SAMPLE INERTNESS RE-PROVED THROUGH THE SHIPPING SITE, not inherited from pjm-168's --set proof: a 2023 keeper replay with nothing forced on the CLI is BIT-IDENTICAL to the committed sidecars (exact frame equality, max|delta| = 0 on all four) with ZERO INADMISSIBLE lines in 2023 — so the arm cannot move PJM's CALIBRATED determination. HELD-OUT EFFECT, measured on the re-run touchpoints (2026-09-07-pjm-2022-2021-touchpoints, folded to the keeper under rule 30): the gate fires in both years dropping exactly 'Average Eastern' and 'Average Western' and un-applying the joint EMAAC cut; EMAAC VOLL 99,100 MWh/74 h -> 0 (2021) and 42,582 MWh/45 h -> 0 (2022); the inverted EMAAC-rest wedge collapses +$20.95 -> +$1.21 and +$15.29 -> +$1.36 against an actual -$5.43; C3b 2021 FAIL (NRMSE 0.355) -> PASS and C3a 2021 +25.7% -> +10.8%. BOTH RUNGS STILL READ NOT-YET (C1 CC_REGULAR over-runs both years, C3a 2021, C3b 2022 0.250 -> 0.257): the arm repairs a real input defect, it does not close 2022. Rule 30(c) — a held-out year never downgrades the ISO; PJM's headline is UNCHANGED at CALIBRATED and the keeper is UNPROMOTED. Evidence: results/calibration/FINDING-pjm169-f2-arm-and-touchpoints-2026-09-06.md; screen: FINDING-pjm168-f1-f2-screens-2026-09-06.md §2." },
